{
  "$comment": "AEP-0002 Annex A machine-usable mapping fixture for the Kimi Code CLI table — the 16-event external-hooks surface -> core types + the vendor-extension fallback. Verified against the pinned vendor source (MoonshotAI/kimi-code c2d7beb = the shipped @moonshot-ai/kimi-code 0.28.1, npm latest and repo head version equal): agent-core-v2 externalHooks/types.ts (the 16-event enum), externalHooksService.ts both scopes (per-event stdin payloads, snake_cased at spawn), approval.ts + permissionGateService.ts (the permission pair). The six lifecycle payload shapes (SessionStart / UserPromptSubmit / PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop / SessionEnd) are ORACLE-CAPTURED from the shipped binary driven headless against a mock provider; the permission pair is source-derived, live-pending. Each entry pins the pure hook->event mapping at the adapter default posture (capture metadata; attention.* redacted). Envelope identity, run synthesis, the permission-pair companions (resolved + the rejected decision's tool.denied by:runtime), the stale-run drain, and the opt-in held PreToolUse gate (AEP_KIMI_CONTROL=1, binary allow/deny) are runtime state, pinned by the reference adapter smokes. Coverage honesty, pinned here as behaviors: PermissionResult decision 'error' degrades to the fallback (an internal gate failure, not an answer); a steer submission never opens a run; the pre-compaction moment degrades to the fallback because the POST moment is the truthful carrier (the CC/Qwen post-moment rule); Notification is background-task status only (never an attention loop); hooks register ONLY in the one global config.toml (strict four-field schema, no per-project file, fail-open by vendor design).",
  "identity": {
    "session_from": "session_id",
    "run_from": null,
    "$comment": "session_id defaults to 'unknown' when absent (SubagentStart/SubagentStop carry none). Hooks carry no turn id at the run boundary: the adapter synthesizes one run per UserPromptSubmit, closed by Stop/StopFailure/Interrupt (the vendor's own Esc moment) and drained at the next boundary when left open. tool_call_id pairs tool and permission moments exactly; PermissionRequest/Interrupt carry turn_id but it never becomes the run id (one id authority, the synthesized run). cwd (workstation-local) deliberately never rides."
  },
